'''Nyiyaparli''' (Nyiyabali, Njijabali, or misspelled ''Nijadali'') is a nearly extinct [[Pama–Nyungan languages|Pama–Nyungan language]] spoken by the [[Palyku]] (Bailko) and [[Niabali]] (Jana) people of [[Western Australia]]. There is also a formal [[language register]] known as ''padupadu''.

